meta {
  name: checkout
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/public/bookings/checkout/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // UUID of the chosen teacher (booking step 1). Required.
    // Must be an active teacher -- see the "teachers" request.
    "teacher": "1e54776b-9910-4742-9f8c-8efd23912d4a",

    // UUID of the package being bought (booking step 2). Required.
    // A package with "is_first_lesson": true can only be bought once per email.
    "package": "2da599cd-ed31-4aa1-b919-0828e1f2e2e9",

    // Start of the first class (booking step 3). Required, ISO-8601 with offset.
    // Copy a "start_utc" straight from the "teacher slots" response -- the slot
    // is re-validated here, so a stale one is rejected rather than double-booked.
    "start_datetime": "2026-09-10T13:00:00+00:00",

    // --- booking step 4: student details ---

    // Required.
    "first_name": "Marco",

    // Optional.
    "last_name": "Reyes",

    // Required. Identifies the account: an existing student is reused, a new one
    // is created and the generated password is emailed to them.
    "email": "marco.reyes@example.com",

    // Optional.
    "phone_number": "+49 170 1234567",

    // Optional.
    "country": "Germany",

    // Optional, defaults to "none". One of:
    // "none", "beginner", "intermediate", "upper_intermediate", "advanced".
    "spanish_level": "beginner",

    // Optional IANA timezone, defaults to "America/Guayaquil". Stored on the
    // student profile and used to render every date back to them.
    "timezone": "Europe/Berlin",

    // --- booking step 5: payment ---

    // Optional. Phase 1 runs the dummy gateway, so any value succeeds --
    // except the literal "declined", which exercises the failure branch.
    "payment_method": "pm_card_visa"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  The entire public booking flow -- steps 1 to 6 -- in one call. No login needed.

  In a single transaction it validates the slot, finds or creates the User +
  Student, creates the purchase, charges the gateway, books the first class and
  issues the invoice. If anything fails, nothing is left behind.

  After the commit it creates the Google Calendar event (falling back to the
  teacher's static Meet room if Calendar is unavailable), emails the confirmation,
  the credentials for a brand-new account and the teacher's new-booking notice,
  then queues the 24h reminder and the 1h follow-up.

  `classes_remaining` is what is left *after* this first class, so a 1-class
  package reports 0. `account_created` tells the frontend whether to show
  "check your email for your password".

  Common 400s -- all as `{"success": false, "message": "..."}`:

  - "That slot has just been taken. Please choose another."
  - "The teacher is not available at that time."
  - "That time is too soon. Please choose a later slot."
  - "The discounted first lesson can only be purchased once. Please choose another package."
  - "Card was declined (dummy gateway)."

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Your lesson is booked. Check your email for the details.",
    "booking": {
      "student_package_id": "534a4812-5ff0-4ba1-a136-ab610f9c9e21",
      "session_id": "fd36207a-5413-48bc-809e-f5d229d971bb",
      "package_title": "Spanish Assessment & First Lesson",
      "teacher": "Fernando Cordero",
      "start_datetime": "2026-09-10T08:00:00-05:00",
      "start_local": "2026-09-10T15:00:00+02:00",
      "timezone": "Europe/Berlin",
      "duration_minutes": 60,
      "meet_link": "https://meet.google.com/abc-defg-hij",
      "amount_paid": "12.00",
      "currency": "USD",
      "invoice_number": "VV-2026-00002",
      "classes_remaining": 0,
      "account_created": true
    }
  }
}
